ip">Alyattes was king of Lydia from around 610 to 560 BCE, of the Mermnad dynasty, and father of Croesus.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/alzey"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alzey.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Alzey</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Alzey is a town in Rhineland-Palatinate, Germany, in the hills of Rhenish Hesse south-west of Mainz.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/amadeo-i-of-spain"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/amadeo-i-of-spain.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Amadeo I of Spain</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Amadeo I, a son of Victor Emmanuel II of Italy, was elected King of Spain by the Cortes and reigned from 1871 to 1873.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/amadeus-aba"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/amadeus-aba.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Amadeus Aba</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Amadeus Aba was a Hungarian baron of the Aba kindred and one of the great oligarchs who ruled provinces almost independently around 1300.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/amadeus-v-count-of-savoy"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/amadeus-v-count-of-savoy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Amadeus V, Count of Savoy</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Amadeus V, called the Great, was Count of Savoy from 1285 until his death in 1323.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/amadeus-vi-count-of-savoy"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/amadeus-vi-count-of-savoy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Amadeus VI, Count of Savoy</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Amadeus VI, known as the Green Count from the colour he wore at tournaments, ruled Savoy from 1343 to 1383.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/amadeus-vii-count-of-savoy"><span class="enc-name">Amadeus VII, Count of Savoy</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Amadeus VII, called the Red Count, was count of Savoy from 1383 to 1391.</span></a></li></ul>
